# Expected output from `buff check examples/use-cases/cli_tool.buff`
#
# Analysis based on the check.rs pipeline (lex → parse → TypeInferencer → naming_lint)
# and prelude_types.rs / import resolution.
#
# STATUS: FAIL — import cannot be resolved (App is a framework crate, not a prelude type)
#
# What the file exercises:
#   - `import App from buff.cli` (framework crate import)
#   - App builder API: App.new("name"), .version(), .about(), .command(), .flag(), .option(), .arg(), .parse()
#   - ParsedArgs accessors: .subcommand(), .subcommand_args(), .flag(), .option(), .arg()
#   - Command dispatch via match on subcommand name (Some("parse"), Some("transform"), etc.)
#   - Option-returning getters: .or(default:) for defaults
#   - String methods: .upper(), .lower(), .reverse(), .split(separator:), .pad_end(width:, fill:)
#   - String interpolation: "{text!r}" (repr), "{label}: {body}"
#   - match on string literals (Some("parse"), _, etc.)
#
# What buff check would report:
#   Lex:     OK (all tokens valid)
#   Parse:   OK (all syntax valid)
#   Modules: FAIL — "import App from buff.cli" cannot resolve
#            (buff-cli is a framework crate, not registered as an import target)
#   Types:   Skipped (module resolution failed)
#   Lint:    Skipped (module resolution failed)
#   Overall: FAIL (import resolution error)
#
# If imports were resolved, the type-level analysis would report:
#   - App.new("textool") → App (associated function)
#   - .command("parse", about:) → Command (builder)
#   - .flag("verbose", short:, description:) → Builder (fluent)
#   - .option("op", short:, description:) → Builder
#   - .arg("input", description:) → Builder
#   - app.parse(Args.all()) → ParsedArgs
#   - parsed.subcommand() → Option<String>
#   - parsed.flag("verbose") → Bool
#   - parsed.option("op") → Option<String>
#   - parsed.arg("input") → Option<String>
#   - .or(default:) → T (resolves the Option)
#
# Pure functions (to_upper, to_lower, reverse, apply_transform) are
# independently testable and would pass buff check in isolation.
#
# This file is a FORWARD-DECLARED specification of the intended user surface.
# It feeds the T8 codegen task and is NOT expected to pass buff check until
# buff-cli's import path is registered.
